Advisory linebreaks for events eligible for selective style overrides.

The features file enables ASS_FEATURE_ADVISORY_LINEBREAKS through compare's
ASS_TEST_FEATURES environment variable. DejaVu Sans is loaded from the shared
.fonts directory; no system fonts are used. The 35-pixel style represents text
enlarged by a consuming application. No renderer style override is needed to
exercise this track feature.

wrap0 through wrap3 cover the script WrapStyle values, preserved and dropped
breaks, soft escapes, empty lines, surrounding spaces, and unbreakable words.
inline covers q changes, resets, spaces across style tags, nonbreaking spaces,
consecutive breaks, styled text, and bidirectional text. excluded covers the
positioning/drawing tags and scrolling effects excluded from selective style
overrides. bidi checks that a retained break is shaped as a space, allowing an
RLO to continue across the line boundary. Event Name fields identify each case.
Each PNG is 320x288; its timestamp selects one event.

retry checks that ignoring hard breaks is accepted only when it produces fewer
lines. Ties preserve authored breaks across all wrap styles, including q2 soft
escapes, spaces across tags, and multiple hard breaks. The last event checks a
retry that does reduce line count. The inline cases with different styles at
breaks, nonbreaking spaces, and bidirectional text also preserve breaks on ties.

Reference provenance:
The .ass.reference files describe the expected output using ordinary ASS with
the feature disabled. They are ignored by compare. PNGs were generated from
these files, not from the feature-enabled test inputs. To reconstruct them,
copy the .ass.reference files to a temporary directory, dropping the .reference
suffix; also copy the PNGs there for their timestamps and dimensions and link
DejaVuSans.ttf. Run compare on that directory with ASS_TEST_FEATURES empty,
-p 3, and -o pointing to this test group. Generation uses the existing PNGs
only for dimensions; the reference ASS supplies all rendered content.

The same PNGs also work with ASS_FEATURE_WRAP_UNICODE and/or
ASS_FEATURE_WHOLE_TEXT_LAYOUT. To check combinations, call compare directly:
ASS_TEST_FEATURES='ADVISORY_LINEBREAKS WRAP_UNICODE WHOLE_TEXT_LAYOUT' compare selective-wrap -p 0
run-single.sh instead uses the group's features file.

Literal LF inside a synthetic event cannot be represented in an ASS file and
is not covered by these file-based fixtures.
